# Builder display copy for supplementary SC13–SC34 (Old Testament), one entry per SD row.
# Built in checkpoints: this file currently covers SC13–SC17 (coverage-ot-history.md).
# Wording follows the accepted research row (supplementary-dispositions/declaration-dispositions.csv,
# minimum_retained_source_context): the quoted summary becomes the first sentence, and the row's
# constraint is kept where it tells a reader something (a distinction, an unresolved identity, a
# separate account). Constraints that only govern drawing ("no coordinate", "do not animate") are
# honoured by drawing nothing. Nothing is added from memory.
#
# Sources: SC13 rows carry their own links. SC14–SC17 rows cite chapter-ledger ids (OH-G11, OH-K1-03,
# OH-S2-15–20 …) instead of links; build.py resolves each id through the ledger rows of
# coverage-ot-history.md, which link the official chapter, so those cards cite chapters, not verses.
#
# Format: SD id -> (card key, display name, desc). Keys are the row's research id; rows whose research
# id is a primary-record code (P18, AP01, AJ01, AE03 …) get an `OTS-` prefix so they never collide
# with the primary card of that code.

